  Few people do.  It's not easy to work out.  Mainly it's learning to
read: <http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/weap-343.txt>  You also
need to learn what missile weapons are multishot and whether they need a
launcher.

  The basic formula is:

             <base damage> + <skill bonus> + <strength bonus> 
Daggers          2.5          2.0 @expert       2.0 @Str:18   = 6.5
Quarterstaff     3.5          2.0 @expert       2.0 @Str:18   = 7.5

  But wait, there's more!  Thrown daggers at expert will average 2.0
daggers per fling.  So you could be averaging 13 damage per move out to
range 9.  Start firing at range 9 and you can sometimes hit the monster
without it reacting.  (I.e. it won't charge at you.)  It was lovely
doing that to a mind-flayer.  If it does charge you can soften it up a
lot even if you don't kill it.  Enough so that your wielded dagger can
easily take care of it while your shield helps you take less damage.


