  If you think weapons choice for a Wizard is difficult, wait until you
try a Priest.  "Priests are restricted from edged weapons but are
good with bludgeons and missiles."  (That "good with...missiles" is not
true, btw.  Priests can't get past basic with any multishot missile.)

  BION, I recommend spears.  They can be used wielded and thrown
(although they are not multishot).  A silver spear can always be wished
for from the Castle wand.  (That average +10.5 silver damage is great 
vs "...all were-creatures (in both human and creature form); all
vampires (V); all demons (&) except Death, Pestilence, Famine, the mail
daemon, djinn, and sandestins; shades; and all imps (i) except tengu.")

  Valks are another class that are great for throwing daggers.  They
start with a +0 dagger and basic skill.  Since thrown daggers are a
"no-hands" weapon you can wield whatever you like.  I heartily recommend
you try throwing daggers early and often.  Even at basic skill they can
be effective at softening up monsters, if you start throwing early
enough.

  If you get Gauntlets of Power throwing Expert daggers will give 2x the
+6 strength damage bonus.  That's 21 damage per fling before you start
enchanting.  (That also works for wizard.)  Averaging 21 per fling will
chew up an approaching monster.  Once it's at melee distance you'll
fight a weakened monster for almost no cost.  (Even at basic if you
start throwing early enough you can hit the monster with a lot of
daggers before it gets to melee range.  Remember, it's the total hits
before the monster reaches melee range that count.)

  (GoP for an early wizard are another reason to throw Expert daggers.
They'll get the same 21 damage per fling that Valks would get.  In fact,
the single best find for most early characters seems to get GoP.)
